  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 4.00,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "Both sides' accounts converge, and the record decides the case. The pickup was 'NEX Serangoon, Tower B ride-hail pickup' (venue VEN-NEX-SERANGOON), a LARGE_VENUE zone, so the POL-NS-02 arrival radius is 120 m and the POL-NS-01 minimum dwell is 300 seconds. The GPS trace (EV-GPS-09105, weight 1.0, 34 fixes, 100% coverage, max_gap_sec 0.0) shows the driver holding a single constant position 219.77 m from the pin at 0.0 km/h for the whole 330-second window from 13:05:00 to 13:10:30. He never entered the 120 m arrival radius — the arrival block reports 0 qualifying in-radius fixes and 0 runs, and longest_qualifying_run.duration_sec is 0.0 against the 300 s minimum. POL-NS-01 limb (b) therefore fails and limb (c) fails with it; the SGD 4.00 fee is not chargeable on the baseline test. Because the driver was nonetheless stationary for the required dwell at 219.77 m — outside the arrival radius but inside the 400 m wrong-entrance ceiling — POL-NS-02 yields to POL-NS-03, which refunds the cancellation fee to the rider in full. On fault for compensation: the chat log (EV-CHAT-09105, weight 1.0) shows the rider naming the correct sub-location at 13:05:05 ('I am at Tower B ride-hail pickup, beside the blue sign') and repeating 'Please come to Tower B' at 13:06:35, while the driver's only message places him at 'the mall taxi stand'; the driver's own statement concedes he waited at a mall entrance 'but did not move to Tower B'. Under POL-NS-03(i) the driver bears the loss and receives no compensation, so driver_compensation_sgd is null and nothing is netted against the rider's refund. I have weighed the remaining contentions. POL-NS-05 is not engaged: at 13:05:20 the driver was 219.77 m from the pin (under the 300 m trigger) and at 0.0 km/h (under the 15 km/h trigger), so the arrival marker is not false and no POL-NS-05(ii) false-arrival referral attaches — the advocates agree and the record confirms it. POL-NS-04 does not exonerate the rider: her locating message was answered at 13:06:00, 55 seconds later and inside the 120-second window, so POL-NS-04's own closing direction applies and the residual mislocation goes to POL-NS-03, which refunds the fee in any event. The rider's independent POL-NS-06 route to the same outcome (zero effective in-geofence dwell) also holds; the MISSING traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-09105-01 (weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT) removes only the POL-NS-06(i) accumulation option and is not held against either party. No POL-NS-08 limb is engaged: no clock skew (the 13:05:20 'arrived' event sits on the 10-second fix grid), no trace gap, a chat log whose 4 messages match trip_record.chat_message_count, and a SGD 4.00 fee that equals the GREATER of the LARGE_VENUE zone-class fee (SGD 4.00) and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee (SGD 4.00). No POL-NS-09 escalation limb fires: there is no direct contradiction on arrival, dwell or rider presence; disputes_with_counterparty_90d is 0 on both profiles; rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 0; and the POL-NS-07 anti-farming test does not trip (1 no-show termination in 30 days against 120 completed trips, ratio 0.008). The lifetime counters (prior_no_show_flags, prior_disputes_filed, prior_disputes_upheld, rating) are context only under POL-GEN-01 and have carried no weight. The deciding facts are carried by unimpaired artifacts at weight 1.0, so confidence is not capped below the 0.70 floor. Ruling: the SGD 4.00 cancellation fee charged to the rider is refunded in full; the driver receives no compensation.",
